NAME
       join - join lines of two files on a common field

SYNOPSIS
       join [-i] [-a 1|2] [-v 1|2] [-e EMPTY] [-o LIST|auto]
          [-t CHAR] [-1 F] [-2 F] [-j F] [--header]
          [--check-order|--nocheck-order] [-z] file1 file2

DESCRIPTION
       Join the lines of two files sorted on a common field.
       Without -t, fields are separated by runs of blanks and
       output fields by one space.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)

